{"name":"Danger","hex":"#ff0e0e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"danger","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Exposure to likely harm; risk of death or serious injury.","An instance or cause of likely serious harm."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To claim liability.","To imperil; to endanger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/danger"}],"entries":[{"title":"Danger Cave","blocks":[{"text":"Danger Cave is a North American archaeological site located in the Bonneville Basin of western Utah around the Great Salt Lakes region, that features artifacts of the Desert Culture from c. 9000 BC until c. 500 AD. Through carbon-14 dating, it has been determined that there is very little evidence of human life in the Danger Cave area c. 11,000 BP [9000 BC], but there is much evidence of human life by 9000 BP [7000 BC]."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Danger_Cave_UT_-_NHL.jpg/330px-Danger_Cave_UT_-_NHL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danger_Cave","wikidata":"Q5215997"},{"title":"Danger Island, Great Chagos Bank","blocks":[{"text":"Danger Island is the westernmost and the southernmost island of the Great Chagos Bank, which is the world's largest coral atoll structure. It is located in the Chagos Archipelago in the Indian Ocean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Danger_Island_ISS006-E-23425.jpg/330px-Danger_Island_ISS006-E-23425.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danger_Island%2C_Great_Chagos_Bank","wikidata":"Q822031"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Danger_Island_commemorative_plaque.jpg/500px-Danger_Island_commemorative_plaque.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/